":\"d39\"},\"ref\":\"d39\",\"snippet\":\" ... In 2010, Kawakami's first full-length novel, Heaven, won the Murasaki Shikibu Prize for Literature. In 2012, an English translation of her short story \\\"March Yarn\\\" appeared in March was Made of Yarn, which is a collection of essays and stories about the 2011 Tōhoku earthquake and ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mieko_Kawakami\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"b910b2905520aaed9b73d26e0d5cf21ff1adb09153ff463695e93e5dace63491\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"a75faa54cfbe7574f1056f9e24010fff76ce98505b084dbae83f8deecc7abaa2\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"novel translated 25 languages prize shortlist 2010s\",\"view\":\"full\"}]}","role":"tool","tool_call_id":"call_f2ffd972b23e4e2d9ba0e545"},{"content":"I found a strong lead. Chigozie Obioma's novels \"The Fishermen\" (2015) and \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) were shortlisted for the Booker Prize and translated into 30 languages. The Man Booker Prize was established in 2002 (renamed from Booker Prize). Let me verify the details.\n\nThe key facts to verify:\n- \"An Orchestra of Minorities\" (2019) - shortlisted for Booker Prize, translated into 30+ languages\n- In 2019, the Booker Prize was won by \"The Testaments\" by Margaret Atwood (published 2019) - but wait, the question says Book B was released the PRECEDING year\n- Actually, let me reconsider. The 2019 Booker went to \"The Testaments\" and \"Girl, Woman, Other\" (joint winners)\n\nLet me check the Booker Prize 2019 details and the Man Booker Prize establishment.","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Man Booker Prize established 2002 renamed\", \"Booker Prize 2019 winner The Testaments Girl Woman Other\", \"An Orchestra of Minorities Chigozie Obioma Booker shortlist 2019\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_c4b29b4b729643108d656913","index":0,"type":"function"},{"function":{"arguments":"{\"queries\": [\"Chigozie Obioma born city grew up\", \"Chigozie Obioma biography birthplace hometown\"], \"top_k\": 10}","name":"search"},"id":"call_98aff7349080434ba88ad6b9","index":1,"type":"function"}]},{"content":"{\"action_slot_charged\":true,\"executed\":true,\"ok\":true,\"results\":[{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d40\"},\"ref\":\"d40\",\"snippet\":\" ... Man Booker Prize\\n\\nThis prize was initially known as the Booker Prize from 1969 to 2001. The Man Group invested in the prize from 2005 to 2015 renaming it the Man Booker Prize and awarding it every two years. Previously, the Man Booker Prize accepted work from the ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.worldatlas.com/articles/the-most-prestigious-literary-awards-in-the-world.html\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d41\"},\"ref\":\"d41\",\"snippet\":\" ... recipient of the Man Booker Prize in 2006, M.A. 1994\\n*Annie Dillard, Pulitzer Prize–winning writer, 1967, M.A. 1968\\n*Ellen Malcolm, founder of EMILY's List, B.A. 1969\\n*Katy Pyle, artistic director of Ballez, B.A. 2002\\n*Henry S. Taylor, Pulitzer Prize–winning poet, M ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hollins_University\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d6\"},\"ref\":\"d6\",\"snippet\":\" ... Jock Campbell, Charles Tyrrell and Tom Maschler were instrumental in establishing the prize.\\n\\nWhen administration of the prize was transferred to the Booker Prize Foundation in 2002, the title sponsor became the investment company Man Group, which opted to retain \\\"Booker\\\" as part of the official title of ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Booker_Prize\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d42\"},\"ref\":\"d42\",\"snippet\":\" ... The Nobel Prize in Literature honours the universal ability of narrative to sculpt and impact cultures, in addition to recognising particular literary brilliance.\\n\\nYou may also like: 10 Magical Books That Combine Christmas and Fantasy\\n\\n2. Man Booker Prize\\n\\nEstablished in 1969, the Man Booker Prize is a ... \",\"title\":\"https://blueroseone.com/publish/list-of-15-most-prestigious-literary-awards-in-2024/\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d43\"},\"ref\":\"d43\",\"snippet\":\" ... Assassin, to critical acclaim, winning both the Booker Prize and the Hammett Prize in 2000. The Blind Assassin was also nominated for the Governor General's Award in 2000, Orange Prize for Fiction, and the International Dublin Literary Award in 2002. In 2001, Atwood was inducted into Canada ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Atwood\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d44\"},\"ref\":\"d44\",\"snippet\":\" ... It was known as either the Orange Prize for Fiction or the Orange Broadband Prize for Fiction until the Orange Group dropped its sponsorship in 2012, after the presentation of that year's award. The following year it was funded by a group of private donors and renamed ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.britannica.com/art/Baileys-Womens-Prize-for-Fiction\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d45\"