ssion to evaluate their readmission policies after a mental health withdrawal, renaming the process to \\\"reinstatement\\\", eliminating the reapplication fee, and ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yale_University\"}],\"next_step\":\"Inspect navigation; read a relevant page or change the locating clue.\",\"observation\":{\"first_delivered_source_round\":null,\"prior_deliveries\":0,\"query_key\":\"7ae0d14b11a462d59e90711b34dea1e0bf645f032f24012300bade22111424b9\",\"replay_requested\":false,\"result_fingerprint\":\"c21c23d5340154d17afc2a3d2684df45091bbbedd2c504e52684bc661ea6dec9\",\"semantic_progress\":\"not_measured\"},\"query\":\"Man Booker Prize established 2002 renamed\",\"view\":\"full\"},{\"cached\":false,\"hits\":[{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d49\"},\"ref\":\"d49\",\"snippet\":\" ... For the bulk of the decade, men are the central characters as per usual in most of these winners.\\n\\nAND YET: The last few years almost make up for it entirely, with the huge range of amazing women in The Testaments, Milkman and especially Girl, Woman, Other, in ... \",\"title\":\"https://www.ontheprize.co.uk/blog/the-booker-prize-in-the-2010s\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":false,\"previously_received\":false,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d50\"},\"ref\":\"d50\",\"snippet\":\" ... Published in 2019 by Hamish Hamilton, it follows the lives of 12 characters in the United Kingdom over the course of several decades. The book was the co-winner of the 2019 Booker Prize, alongside Margaret Atwood's The Testaments.\\n\\nGirl, Woman, Other has received more than 30 ... \",\"title\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Girl,_Woman,_Other\"},{\"kind\":\"navigation_not_evidence\",\"navigation_seen\":true,\"previously_received\":true,\"raw_ranges_delivered\":[],\"read_action\":{\"ref\":\"d6\"},\"ref\":\"d6\",\"